{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: RNA-only, singleprofile, PCA → 48.5% acc), the most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality carries independent predictive signal for this task. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest parallel baseline: same profile setting, same simplicity level, but swapping the modality. If image-only performs comparably to RNA-only (~48%), multimodal fusion is unlikely to add much; if it substantially outperforms, the image channel is a strong signal source and multimodal fusion becomes a high-priority direction; if it underperforms, RNA remains the dominant modality and effort should focus on improving RNA representations (scvi, scgpt, multiprofile). This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the core design question—whether to invest in multimodal fusion—before committing budget to more complex configurations that conflate multiple variables."
}

